# `.btcc` files are a byte-exact interchange format, not ordinary text.
#
# `serializeBtcc` always emits LF (see lib/btcc/AGENTS.md and docs/RULES.md §1.1),
# and `lib/btcc/roundtrip.test.ts` asserts `serialize(parse(fixture)) === fixture`
# byte-for-byte against the file as read from disk. Git stores these fixtures with
# LF, but `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, which breaks
# byte-equality and fails the golden tests on a correct working tree.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion for these paths in both directions,
# so the working copy matches what is stored.
*.btcc -text
